  "text": "Recipe: Corn Grits Kolkatte\nCreator: Sharmila Vedam\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: corn grits, carrots, mustard seeds, chana dhal, split urad dal, curry leaves, green chilies, shredded coconut, cilantro, turmeric powder, hot water, salt\nCooking methods: dry roast, steam\nInstructions: Dry roast mustard seeds, channa dal, split urad dal & curry leaves together in a pan. Add corn grits & dry roast for 4-5 mins.\nSwitch off the flame. Add shredded coconut & carrots. Add cilantro, turmeric powder & salt (to taste). Give all the ingredients a good mix. Add hot water slowly and keep stirring till it binds together.\nBind the dough into oval shapes or round balls. Steam them for about 20-25 minutes.\nEnjoy with any kind of chutney (today I served it with walnut chutney) but goes best with coconut chutney.\nNotes: Corn grits from Indian grocery stores. Green chilies according to your preference. Shredded coconut is optional. Salt to taste. A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (corn grits), RAINBOW VEGGIES (carrots), NUTS & SEEDS (coconuts), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
